<title>TURKEY: Turkish Otosan H1 profit rise.</title>
<headline>Turkish Otosan H1 profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 7,796.94  vs   2,758.93</p>
<p>    Net profit		 10,861.15  vs   3,641.79</p>
<p>    Net sales		  51,208.16  vs  15,039.44</p>
<p>    Operating profit	 10,980.03  vs   4,398.21</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	5,287.17  vs   1,261.30</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	  80.65  vs	 1.58</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   6.70  vs	 4.21</p>
<p>    Total debts		15,572.41  vs   6,213.70</p>
<p>    Equity		     21,503.26  vs   7,962.41</p>
<p>    Capital		     1,392.50  vs   1,320.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish passenger car and commercial vehicle producer Otosan Otomobil Sanayii A.S is owned 41.035 percent by Turkey's leading industrial Koc group and 41.035 percent by Ford Motor Co.</p>
<p>It changed its named to Ford Otomotiv Sanayi A.S on July 24, after equalised their equities on June 30.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
